  "body": "Adds injectable trusted-contact and privacy UI for the existing shared app. Drivers can list their own contacts, request explicit scopes and revoke standing sharing. A contact can read a known trip\u2019s protected location, read a known incident, record an acknowledgement or their own action, and revoke a known trip grant. Uncertain writes retain the original key/body for explicit retry; protected facts disappear before revoke and on session replacement. Acknowledgement, reported action, source-aged location, unknown delivery and driver-only resolution remain separate.\n\nFrozen candidate: `e2c1e677cf3ec3fa9c7f91529b082ab5b8ff91e6`. The latest commit changes 14 owned files; the complete PR stays within `web/src/features/contacts/**`, `web/src/features/privacy/**` and matching tests. Base remains Robert\u2019s backend `ebc8fb1d36f441ef012ca585201cefabf61383d6`. Shared foundation, API, package/lock, router, entry and backend files are not copied or changed here.\n\n`createContactRoutes({api,session,gateway,incidentReference?,grantReference?})` supplies the four approved registry slots: contacts, invitation, contactTrip and privacy. It consumes foundation PR56 `3283fe675ebeee04bb2be8a62f42ab5c475b4b0e` and API PR59 `db7034fc9e1dba035b87368117376e9730d6b830`. The host must share one API/MemorySession/gateway and separately activate each feature\u2019s verified `/v1/me` binding. The contact-only trip selector permits a null driver identity without inventing one; owner selection and driver resolution guards are unchanged. UUID hints provide no permission and never render incident facts without the protected read and trip match.\n\nIncoming invitation metadata and contact trip/incident discovery remain unpublished. The invitation page therefore explains that requested scopes cannot yet be reviewed and keeps acceptance unavailable; participant-authorized withdrawal can use the known route grant ID. The owner catalog follows PR65 exact `748d30c6e6c595fd1a2c2c648a045750de3dd9c8`, preserves historical accepted/revoked scopes and truncation, and is not incoming invitation discovery. Robert/44 must coordinate the remaining reads and planned status/sharing contracts. No lookup, DTO, emergency number, permission, history, research or notification capability is invented. Route disposal clears local command/receipt state without reconciling or cancelling an unknown server outcome; the UI says leaving does not cancel it and claims no persisted operation history.\n\nValidation on Node24.17.0 / TypeScript5.9.3: 22 standalone journey/privacy tests and 6 tests through the actual typed client/gateway/binding pass. The existing 3 signed-JWT/PostgreSQL scenarios pass again with a fresh private Unix-socket cluster, which was stopped and removed. The composed foundation build and strict source/fixture typecheck pass. Browser builder evidence covers 40 route/locale/viewport cases (ES/PT-BR at390/1440/1920/360/430px) plus13 focused controls/states: trusted keyboard, input/scope validation, duplicate-submit suppression, separate receipts and escaped reports, session clearing, rejected same-key retry, permission/error/empty/truncated states, missing references, reduced motion and the narrow phone response action. Viewport/full-page captures are supplied for independent review. Whitespace checks pass.\n\nReproduce from the owned README using `node web/tests/contacts/compose-ui.mjs`; it archives the immutable shared dependencies into a disposable folder and copies only owned feature/tests, recording source HEAD/working state. Its development-only fixture renders the real foundation/API/controller with synthetic in-memory HTTP replies and identities. Those browser/client checks are not browser OIDC, persisted UI reload, physical-device, provider delivery or independent acceptance evidence. The normal production entry still needs integrator44 to mount this registry with a trusted host and the actual backend read routes. The existing backend persisted tests are distinct from the synthetic UI fixture. Production build success currently compiles the new components; it does not claim the default entry registers them or establishes their production bundle cost.\n\nEarlier fix evidence stays bounded: [Q45 closed its original retry-state finding at b95bdba](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/62#issuecomment-6243021647), and [Q43\u2019s subsequent review explicitly covers5c15183](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/62#pullrequestreview-5560631743), superseding its e78-only pass. The two README spacing nits from that review are fixed. Neither acceptance is promoted to this new UI/observation bridge. Fresh exact-SHA auth/privacy43 and functional UI52 reviews are required, along with shared dependency reviews. Component44 alone integrates after all live discussion, inline threads, formal COMMENTED findings and relevant issue feedback are resolved and Robert\u2019s separate approval is obtained. No merge, main push, deployment, collection or live sends occurred.\n\nRefs #15\nRefs #35\nRefs #14\n",
